    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d411">

                <pb facs="0566" n="454" xml:id="pg454"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/7442: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Neville</hi>)<anchor n="61" xml:id="d411-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-11-29T15:00:00-05:00">November 29, 1935—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>185. Under date November 27 the American Embassy at London telegraphed as
                    follows:</p>
                <p>[Here follows quotation of first paragraph of telegram No. 595, November 27, 1
                    p.m., printed on <ref target="#pg448">page 448</ref>.]</p>
                <p>This morning the British Ambassador here gave us the same information.</p>
                <p>In neither case was any suggestion made that this Government take similar or any
                    action.</p>
                <p>Department would welcome any comments which you may feel moved to make.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d411-f1" n="61" type="source" xml:id="d411-f1-content">
                <p>The same to the Ambassador in China as telegram No. 63, November 29, 2 p.m.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
